# 🏏 IPL Cricket Analytics System

## Setup

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Terminal 1 — Start API
uvicorn main:app --reload

# Terminal 2 — Start Dashboard
streamlit run app.py
```

Visit `http://localhost:8501` for the dashboard.
API docs at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.

Login: **admin / admin123**

---

## Database Justification

**PostgreSQL (OLTP)** was chosen because:
- The system supports full CRUD (player notes, future bookings/team selection)
- ACID guarantees matter for consistent stat reads and writes
- Foreign key relationships between players, teams, and matches enforce data integrity
- Historical IPL data (~hundreds of thousands of rows) is well within PostgreSQL's range

An OLAP store (DuckDB/ClickHouse) would be faster for pure aggregations over millions of rows, but since this system includes transactional writes (scout notes, team management), a hybrid approach would be the production path: PostgreSQL as the operational store + a materialized view or DuckDB layer for dashboard queries.

---

## Guideline Compliance

| Requirement | Status |
|---|---|
| Real-world dataset with enough volume | ✅ IPL ball-by-ball data |
| Relational DB with justified choice | ✅ PostgreSQL (OLTP justified above) |
| Schema with multiple tables | ✅ ipl_raw, ipl_matches, ipl_players, ipl_player_stats, ipl_bowler_stats, ipl_teams, player_notes |
| FastAPI with CRUD endpoints | ✅ Full Create/Read/Update/Delete on player_notes |
| Pydantic models for validation | ✅ All request/response models validated |
| Authentication | ✅ JWT via OAuth2PasswordBearer |
| ≥3 analytics endpoints | ✅ 8 analytics endpoints |
| API docs via /docs | ✅ Auto-generated |
| ≥3 visualizations in dashboard | ✅ Bar, scatter, histogram, pie, radar charts |
| Dashboard refresh logic | ✅ Manual refresh button (justified: static historical data) |
| ≥1 interactive filter/element | ✅ Season filter, min-balls slider, player search |

---

## Endpoints Summary

### Auth
- `POST /auth/login` — Get JWT token

### Analytics (all require Bearer token)
- `GET /top-players` — Top batters (filterable by min_balls, limit)
- `GET /top-bowlers` — Top wicket-takers
- `GET /top-teams` — Team run totals
- `GET /matches-per-team` — Match counts
- `GET /player-of-match` — POM award leaders
- `GET /seasons` — Available seasons
- `GET /team-wins-by-season` — Win counts (filterable by season)
- `GET /player-search` — Search by name, returns batting + bowling stats

### CRUD — Player Notes
- `POST /notes` — Create note
- `GET /notes` — Read notes (filterable by player name)
- `PUT /notes/{id}` — Update note
- `DELETE /notes/{id}` — Delete note